  "body": "## Status: recursive-interface research construction/correction; no new kappa\n\nPR1155's frozen restoration-coalescing note says read-freedom is necessary for deferred dirty-workspace restoration. Its bad-reader example establishes that unrestricted deferral can fail, not that every reader fails. This independent package supplies the exact criterion in its stated additive model:\n\n`sum_i B_i (G_{i-1}...G_1 - I) = 0`.\n\nThe written proof covers arbitrary dimensions and fields, while the executable evidence is explicitly finite. Prefix observations require each prefix defect to vanish; terminal cancellation alone is not safe for adaptive observations.\n\n- Nonzero invariant-reader shear batches permit genuine restoration elimination. The seed-selected five-child family pays **15N -> 11N** scalar ADDs per node, including readers, forward drift and final restoration.\n- A second example reads the changing coordinate and cancels its two observable defects only at the endpoint, separating terminal and prefix contracts.\n- Complete recursion, scalar/memory-access invoices, child calls, descriptor/controller charges, integer magnitude bounds and storage limits are stated. An actual recursive event emitter is replayed forward and inverse on every dirty-state basis column in its bounded domain.\n- Independent block-state multiplication checks the defect formula on all **46,656** three-child signed-reader/shear tuples. Noncommuting rational evidence and six mathematical controls are included, plus standalone relocation and a real source-corruption rejection.\n\n### Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/observer-safe-restoration/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected final marker: `PASS_OBSERVER_RESTORATION_PACKAGE relocation=1 source_corruption=1`.\n\nBase `1b59b624d21924f8e3537cdc1ac52d3be6eda2fe`; OS assignment seed **52**. PR1155 source pinned at `9821c6e9388f3fc097e94b72be9fa7b41a849527`, with its complete README preserved and authenticated. The selected PR1094 construction, upstream/, and all existing supplier code are untouched. No selected cold replay, hosted supplier admission, compiler/tape realization, remote CI, full formal proof, or stronger multiplication exponent is claimed.\n\nCredits Aaron Wang (@navinor), PR1155, and its retained restoration-interface predecessors. Distinct from PR889 common-factor query batching, PR1105 projected target-feedback cleanup, PR1012 hosted restoration mass, and PR1135 rounded borrowing. Fresh overlap metadata and the local claim are included; no pinned coordination issue was present. Prepared by Adam Gall (@adamgall), with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; existing license and attribution retained.\n",
